       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. As written, it's a dose I think you should double-check.\n\n**Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** That's twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day. The labeled single-dose maximum for prescription ibuprofen is 800 mg, so 1600 mg per dose is also double that. Even with normal kidney and liver function, this dose carries a meaningful risk of GI bleeding, renal injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nCommon regimens for this patient would be:\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO every 8 hours** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n\nWhich did you intend? Or, if 6,400 mg/day is deliberate, please confirm and I'll enter it with a note documenting the rationale. I'll also add a note about the indication and duration if you tell me those."
      }
     ],
